h the  server room if you download the app this  is the screen you get it's a typical OS  X you just right drag it into  applications and launch it and you'll  have a server running on your computer  once it's running this is what it looks  like you get a welcome screen with a  sidebar things are kind of bucketed into  sessions so that you can keep track of  visualizations that you've made but the  cool thing is you can see this page all  the visualizations that are in here so  each one of these is something that you  can send data to and have it display  with your data and then you can click  through and see exactly what that looks  like and you can even like since these  are all JavaScript modules you can use  this page to import new ones or custom  ones that you make and at the end I'll  go through an example of doing that this  is a Python setup it's pretty easy  hopefully everyone is familiar with this  if you don't like pip you can clone it  from it's not github searching lightning  is Python will give you that link so  here's the first kind of simplest Python  example okay so first two lines are just  importing the libraries the second one  where we instantiate the client LG N  equals lightning we pass in the host so  I don't have a server running locally  for this example but I pass in this  public URL so that tells it use that as  my backing server then I create some  random data I'm using numb PI's random  function and I plot a line plot so that  line V equals LG n dot line is what's  actually plotting it we get a reference  to the plot and then we can call it open  and we'll open it in your browser like  this and since we're using the public  server like you have a link that you can  send to people now these are all on the  public server they're all anonymized and  in the same way that github gist's work  like secret gists so no one can find  your visualizer  but if you share the link then people  will be able to access them and so in in  this line here n