ion and  then a function to transform data if you  need it to be transformed in any way so  for example this is just a JavaScript  charting library called chart.js  if you wanted to plug this in to  lightning and start like creating plots  from your Python code what you would do  is you would have this structure and  then you'd go in let's say you  essentially you would fill in the init  function which is it needs a canvas on  the screen so I draw a canvas and you  fill in the render function it needs to  be initialized with this chart library  JavaScript and then you can just go to  this screen on your server and type in  the module name I just called it I think  lightning custom example for this one  just because it was a test but what this  is going to do when I hit submit is it  goes on to NPM it pulls down the package  it compiles it and brings it into your  Lightning server environment and then  you're going to be able to start using  it in interacting with it in the same  way that you can interact with it with  all the default visualizations so like  that live editor that you saw before and  like the Python API is will exist so it  takes a few like 10 or 20 seconds to  actually come in but now you have this  visualization that lightning is  rendering you can actually go in and  it's all alive you can change the data  and you can call this from Python it's  like just completely in the ecosystem  now and it's really really easy to like  get it in there which is the idea of  this whole thing let's see  oh yeah that is what I have for you  I went over pretty quickly all of the  kind of high-level functionality so if  anyone has particular questions I'd be  happy to answer them  so there's hemp two answers is like one  if it's already exposed through like the  options parameters you can just pass it  and through Python it if it's something  that that does that doesn't work the  process would be like you clone the  version of it that's on github locally  you make y